      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 field answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-8454: the fourth-quadrant argument is 2\\pi-\\arctan(5/7), approximately 5.66. q-38999: exclude x=0 because its denominator vanishes. q-81297: exclude x=1/5 because 5x-1=0. q-81306: k(4/5)-4=0 gives k=5. q-40027: 3(-4)+b=0 gives b=12. q-81416: 1/(x-6) takes every nonzero real value, so adding 1 gives every real value except 1. q-73156: the width is 2e/n and left endpoints are e+2ie/n, with i=0,...,n-1. q-73180: the width is 5/n and right endpoints are -2+5k/n, with k=1,...,n. q-112815: 7x^2(x+6) has only x=0 as a double root. q-178256: (x-5)^2(x+5) has only x=5 as a double root. q-100997: 3e+f=(-2,7,-3), so d-(3e+f)=(11,0,7). q-98142: the coordinate differences have magnitudes 4w, giving distance sqrt(48w^2)=4\\sqrt{3}w since w>0. q-141812: roots -2 and 10 give squared sum 104. q-142015: roots 3 and 7 give squared sum 58. q-12997: completing the square gives (a+4)^2=64, so p+q=68 and a=-12 or 4. q-112457: completing the square gives (t-7)^2=49, so pq=-343; roots 0 and 14 sum to 14. Confirmation is based on captured worked solutions; no submitted grades or prior answers were supplied.",
